# Copy to `.env.local`. Never commit `.env.local`.
#
# Every variable is REQUIRED and has no default. src/server/config.ts validates them when the
# server starts, and `next dev` / `next start` exits naming each missing or malformed one and
# why, never its value. A variable set to nothing counts as missing.
#
# None of them is NEXT_PUBLIC_*: nothing here is inlined into the browser's bundle. The one
# value the browser needs, the tile URL, reaches it as a prop the server hands the map.

# APP_ENV — one of: local | development | staging | production
#
# The same four names the backend and the player app use (docs/environments.md). **Only
# `local` runs today.** Outside `local` the session cookie is `Secure`, and the tile URL must
# be https://.
APP_ENV=local

# API_URL — the backend, called from this server and never from the browser. Server to
# server, so no scheme rule. The backend's dev stack answers here (backend/docker-compose-local.yml).
API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# SESSION_SECRET — seals the session cookie (and the Forgot password? cookie). At least 32
# characters. Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# Changing it signs every club out, which is the way to do that on purpose.
SESSION_SECRET=

# MAP_TILE_URL — the map's tile template, with {z}, {x} and {y}. The browser fetches it, so
# it is https:// in every deployed environment. OpenStreetMap's own tile servers are for
# development only: production traffic needs a provider that allows it, which is a deploy-time
# item (ADR-0187 §3). Keep the attribution the map shows when you change it.
MAP_TILE_URL=https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png

# MAP_START — where the sign-up map opens before a pin is dropped: latitude,longitude in
# decimal degrees. Kraków's centre.
MAP_START=50.0614,19.9366

# GEOCODER_URL — the address search over the map: a typed address becomes a pin. Nominatim's
# /search, or anything answering its jsonv2 shape. Called from this server, never from the
# browser, so no scheme rule. Nominatim's own server allows light use only (one request a
# second, the caller identified — the website does both); production traffic needs a provider
# that allows it, which is a deploy-time item, as the tiles' is (ADR-0187 §3).
GEOCODER_URL=https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search
